    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "txt_0344",
      "reading_order": 398,
      "section": "Electrical Shock Hazard",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 107.4117,
        "t": 615.0682318,
        "r": 218.18509379999995,
        "b": 606.3907174112267
      },
      "content": "Electrical Shock Hazard",
      "level": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0345",
      "reading_order": 399,
      "section": "Electrical Shock Hazard",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 46.026161699999996,
        "t": 599.9245768000001,
        "r": 253.4063043,
        "b": 580.9884574112267
      },
      "content": "Only authorized technicians should perform diagnostic voltage measurements."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0346",
      "reading_order": 400,
      "section": "Electrical Shock Hazard",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 46.026161699999996,
        "t": 574.5223168000001,
        "r": 237.12931769999994,
        "b": 555.5861974112267
      },
      "content": "After performing voltage measurements, disconnect power before servicing."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0347",
      "reading_order": 401,
      "section": "Electrical Shock Hazard",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 46.026161699999996,
        "t": 549.1200568000002,
        "r": 270.7970823,
        "b": 530.1839374112268
      },
      "content": "Failure to follow these instructions can result in death or electrical shock."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "txt_0348",
      "reading_order": 402,
      "section": "General Theory of Operation",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 35.5,
        "t": 505.862,
        "r": 225.67600000000007,
        "b": 493.6893613445378
      },
      "content": "General Theory of Operation",
      "level": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0349",
      "reading_order": 403,
      "section": "General Theory of Operation",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 35.5,
        "t": 476.08,
        "r": 191.62999999999994,
        "b": 468.4600630252101
      },
      "content": "Refer to Wiring Diagram on page 3-3."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0350",
      "reading_order": 404,
      "section": "General Theory of Operation",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 35.5,
        "t": 450.07,
        "r": 283.79999999999995,
        "b": 392.4621008403361
      },
      "content": "Neutral and L1 (AC voltage) enters the Control Board at CON1, pins 1 & 2 respectively.  AC is converted to DC voltage at the Low Volts Power Supply (LVPS). Supplies include +12 and +5 VDC, and DC GND (REF). These low voltage supplies are used to provide power to the microprocessors and board components, power the sensors and energize the AC relays."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0351",
      "reading_order": 405,
      "section": "General Theory of Operation",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 35.5,
        "t": 387.07,
        "r": 292.3199999999999,
        "b": 289.4621008403361
      },
      "content": "The 12 VDC is vital to the operation of the dishwasher. This supply is necessary to operate all 120 VAC loads in the dishwasher, whether they are connected to a relay or controlled by TRIACs. 12 VDC is generated by the power supply and flows through the door switch-when closed-to be available to the heater relay, wash motor relays, and the drain pump relay.  A relay coil becomes energized when the control closes the LV drive circuit for a specific relay completing 12V pathway, which in turn closes the relay switch providing AC to the load."
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig_0043",
      "reading_order": 406,
      "section": "General Theory of Operation",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 55.8225212097168,
        "t": 45.092041015625,
        "r": 64.52682495117188,
        "b": 35.43292236328125
      },
      "image_path": "figures/figure_0043.png",
      "previous_block_id": "txt_0351",
      "next_block_id": "txt_0352"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0352",
      "reading_order": 407,
      "section": "General Theory of Operation",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 56.1631,
        "t": 44.86829999999998,
        "r": 72.4687,
        "b": 32.765719354838666
      },
      "content": "n"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "txt_0353",
      "reading_order": 408,
      "section": "Power Check",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 303.0,
        "t": 706.112,
        "r": 388.44000000000005,
        "b": 693.9393613445378
      },
      "content": "Power Check",
      "level": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0354",
      "reading_order": 409,
      "section": "Power Check",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 303.0,
        "t": 676.32,
        "r": 556.2300000000001,
        "b": 648.7121008403361
      },
      "content": "This test checks for incoming and outgoing power to and from the control board.  This test assumes that proper voltages is present at the outlet or direct connect cable."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "txt_0355",
      "reading_order": 410,
      "section": "Test Procedure",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 303.0,
        "t": 639.584,
        "r": 376.53600000000006,
        "b": 630.4545210084034
      },
      "content": "Test Procedure",
      "level": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0356",
      "reading_order": 411,
      "section": "Test Procedure",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 309.0,
        "t": 625.82,
        "r": 487.8100000000002,
        "b": 618.2121008403361
      },
      "content": "Unplug dishwasher or disconnect power."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0357",
      "reading_order": 412,
      "section": "Test Procedure",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 309.0,
        "t": 613.32,
        "r": 411.7500000000001,
        "b": 605.7121008403361
      },
      "content": "Remove access panel."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0358",
      "reading_order": 413,
      "section": "Test Procedure",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 309.0,
        "t": 600.82,
        "r": 435.65,
        "b": 593.2121008403361
      },
      "content": "Remove terminal box cover."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0359",
      "reading_order": 414,
      "section": "Test Procedure",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 309.0,
        "t": 588.32,
        "r": 559.98,
        "b": 561.7121008403361
      },
      "content": "With a voltmeter set to AC, insert black probe inside white wire screw nut (N) and insert red probe inside black wire screw nut (L1)."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0360",
      "reading_order": 415,
      "section": "Test Procedure",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 309.0,
        "t": 556.82,
        "r": 482.73000000000013,
        "b": 549.2121008403361
      },
      "content": "Plug in dishwasher or reconnect power."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0361",
      "reading_order": 416,
      "section": "Test Procedure",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 317.0,
        "t": 545.54,
        "r": 556.86,
        "b": 527.2121008403361
      },
      "content": "¾ ¾ If 120 VAC is present, unplug dishwasher or disconnect power and proceed to step 6."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0362",
      "reading_order": 417,
      "section": "Test Procedure",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 317.0,
        "t": 523.54,
        "r": 558.5400000000001,
        "b": 505.2121008403361
      },
      "content": "¾ ¾ If 120 VAC is not present, have customer correct power problem at outlet or breaker."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0363",
      "reading_order": 418,
      "section": "Test Procedure",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 309.0,
        "t": 500.32,
        "r": 452.97,
        "b": 492.7121008403361
      },
      "content": "Remove the control board cover."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0364",
      "reading_order": 419,
      "section": "Test Procedure",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 309.0,
        "t": 487.82,
        "r": 421.7199999999997,
        "b": 480.2121008403361
      },
      "content": "Locate connector CON 1."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0365",
      "reading_order": 420,
      "section": "Test Procedure",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 309.0,
        "t": 475.32,
        "r": 553.0100000000002,
        "b": 458.2121008403361
      },
      "content": "With a voltmeter set to AC, connect leads across the two pins ('N' and 'L') on CON 1."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0366",
      "reading_order": 421,
      "section": "Test Procedure",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 309.0,
        "t": 453.32,
        "r": 482.73000000000013,
        "b": 445.7121008403361
      },
      "content": "Plug in dishwasher or reconnect power."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0367",
      "reading_order": 422,
      "section": "Test Procedure",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 317.0,
        "t": 442.04,
        "r": 478.41,
        "b": 432.7303225806452
      },
      "content": "¾ ¾ If 120 VAC is present, go to step 10."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0368",
      "reading_order": 423,
      "section": "Test Procedure",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 317.0,
        "t": 429.54,
        "r": 557.4100000000002,
        "b": 411.2121008403361
      },
      "content": "¾ ¾ If 120 VAC is not present, check for open connection between terminal block and control. Repair as needed."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0369",
      "reading_order": 424,
      "section": "Test Procedure",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 304.0,
        "t": 406.32,
        "r": 394.38000000000005,
        "b": 398.7121008403361
      },
      "content": "10.\t Verify DC Supplies"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0370",
      "reading_order": 425,
      "section": "Test Procedure",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 303.0,
        "t": 393.32,
        "r": 546.6000000000001,
        "b": 375.7121008403361
      },
      "content": "5 VDC is used to power IC's and micro-processors on the circuit board as well as provide power to the sensors."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0371",
      "reading_order": 426,
      "section": "Test Procedure",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 317.0,
        "t": 371.54,
        "r": 558.5899999999999,
        "b": 332.7121008403361
      },
      "content": "¾ ¾ If 5 VDC were missing, the control and Turbidity Sensor would not function. To verify 5V ± 5%, with a voltmeter set to DC, connect the black lead to CN4-2 (DC GND) and the red lead to CN3-1 (+5V)."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0372",
      "reading_order": 427,
      "section": "Test Procedure",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 303.0,
        "t": 327.32,
        "r": 558.1600000000003,
        "b": 309.7121008403361
      },
      "content": "12 VDC is used to actuate the heater, drain and wash pump relays as well as the dispenser and water inlet valve."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0373",
      "reading_order": 428,
      "section": "Test Procedure",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 317.0,
        "t": 305.54,
        "r": 558.7400000000001,
        "b": 266.7121008403361
      },
      "content": "¾ ¾ If 12 VDC was missing, the heater, pumps, and all other loads would not turn on. To verify 12V ± 5%, with a voltmeter set to DC, connect the red lead to CN6-1 (12V) and black lead to CN4-2 (DC GND)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0374",
      "reading_order": 429,
      "section": "Test Procedure",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 321.0,
        "t": 252.31999999999994,
        "r": 555.9100000000003,
        "b": 184.71210084033612
      },
      "content": "Troubleshooting Missing DC Supplies: Refer to the wiring diagram on page 3-4 when troubleshooting the DC supplies. If 5 VDC or 12 VDC is missing on the control, unplug dishwasher or disconnect power, and then disconnect all components/loads from the control relying on the missing or loaded supply. Plug in dishwasher or reconnect power and check if the DC supply has returned."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0375",
      "reading_order": 430,
      "section": "Test Procedure",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 317.0,
        "t": 180.53999999999996,
        "r": 441.02000000000015,
        "b": 171.23032258064518
      },
      "content": "¾ ¾ If not, replace the control."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0376",
      "reading_order": 431,
      "section": "Test Procedure",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 317.0,
        "t": 167.53999999999996,
        "r": 557.1500000000002,
        "b": 138.71210084033612
      },
      "content": "¾ ¾ If it has, turn off dishwasher and reconnect one connector at a time until the component loading down that supply has been identified."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0377",
      "reading_order": 432,
      "section": "Test Procedure",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 304.0,
        "t": 133.31999999999994,
        "r": 483.47000000000014,
        "b": 125.71210084033612
      },
      "content": "Unplug dishwasher or disconnect power."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0378",
      "reading_order": 433,
      "section": "Test Procedure",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 304.0,
        "t": 120.31999999999994,
        "r": 450.7400000000003,
        "b": 112.71210084033612
      },
      "content": "Reassemble all parts and panels."
    }
  ]
}